{"name":"Buried Treasure","hex":"#d28b42","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buried treasure","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something valuable that is concealed for a long time and then rediscovered.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see buried,‎ treasure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buried_treasure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buried Treasure (1921 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Buried Treasure is a 1921 American silent adventure film directed by George D. Baker and written by George D. Baker and F. Britten Austin. The film stars Marion Davies, Norman Kerry, Anders Randolf, Edith Shayne, Earl Schenck, John Charles, and Thomas Findley. The film was released on April 10, 1921, by Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Buried_Treasure_%281921_film%29_poster.jpg/330px-Buried_Treasure_%281921_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buried_Treasure_(1921_film)","wikidata":"Q2229195"},{"title":"Buried treasure","blocks":[{"text":"Buried treasure is a literary trope commonly associated with depictions of pirates, alongside Vikings, criminals, and outlaws in the Old West. According to popular conception, these people often buried their stolen fortunes in remote places, intending to return to them later."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg/330px-Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buried_treasure","wikidata":"Q4386797"},{"title":"Treasure","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure is a concentration of wealth — often originating from ancient history — that is considered lost and/or forgotten until rediscovered. Some jurisdictions legally define what constitutes treasure, such as in the British Treasure Act 1996."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure","wikidata":"Q272937"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"buried treasure":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/En-au-buried_treasure.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e3/En-au-buried_treasure.ogg/En-au-buried_treasure.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Orange 002 2014 03 19","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Orange_002_2014_03_19.jpg/500px-Orange_002_2014_03_19.jpg","ratio":1.619781631342325,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orange_002_2014_03_19.jpg","share":0.149375},{"title":"Orange-fruit-16x16","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/Orange-fruit-16x16.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":1,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orange-fruit-16x16.jpg","share":0.148125},{"title":"Orange-fruit-32x32","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Orange-fruit-32x32.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":1,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orange-fruit-32x32.jpg","share":0.1225},{"title":"Oranges - whole-halved-segment","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg/500px-Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg","share":0.108125},{"title":"Samanea saman on an island with orange clouds and blue sky at sunrise from Don Det Si Phan Don Laos","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Samanea_saman_on_an_island_with_orang